%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against D32 + D33 + D21
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SYS as ReadyCall
    participant WS as Workstation (browser)
    participant A as Agent
    participant TEL as Telephony
    participant C as Customer
    participant INT as Intake

    SYS->>WS: CallOffered (websocket)
    WS->>A: offer card + ringtone IN THE BROWSER TAB
    Note over WS,A: there is no desk phone. The tab IS the phone. (D32)
    WS->>A: shows who / why / urgency BEFORE accepting

    Note over SYS,INT: the offer window doubles as the intake grace period (D21)
    SYS->>INT: an agent is found - you have ~7s, wrap up cleanly
    INT->>C: "ขอบคุณค่ะ กำลังต่อสายให้"
    INT->>SYS: finalize(partial=true) - a cut-off sentence is still useful

    alt Accept
        A->>WS: clicks Accept
        WS->>TEL: SIP.js answers over WSS
        TEL->>TEL: bridge the caller leg to the agent leg
        SYS->>SYS: OFFERED to IN_CALL
    else Decline
        A->>WS: clicks Decline, with a reason
        SYS->>SYS: OFFERED to MATCHED - re-match someone else
    else No answer (RONA)
        Note over WS,SYS: timeout, about 20s
        SYS->>SYS: OFFERED to MATCHED
        SYS->>WS: flip the agent OUT of Ready
        Note right of SYS: otherwise the same unattended desk<br/>keeps being offered calls
    end
